{"posts":[{"id":"finddecision_p1_1","t":"Price regularly moves from decision point to decision point.\n\nTake a look at this video to see what I mean\n\nWasher\n\nfind\n\n14517\n\nHomework:\n\nThis will be alot like the Read a Session Homework, except that I want you to do learn from it how to pinpoint in advance, turns in the market which will pay you very large rewards for minimal risk.\n\nSo Open a D1 chart on any pair Download as much LTF history as you can for it Start at the second price turn on the left Look to the left of it, in the lowest TF you can Work out why price reacted to that level Mark the reason on the LTF chart Take a little screenshot of that area - name it \"name of pair\"1 Mark the turning point on D1 with a 1 Move on to the next turning point, and repeat, and then the next. Do this for every turning point. When you're finished, you'll have a D1 chart with all the turning points numbered, and a gallery of thumbnails of the LTFs, each explaining the turns.\n\nDo this for as many pairs as you possibly can\n\nBelieve me, it'll be well worth it!","a":"—","d":"","n":"#1","p":1,"im":[],"m":1},{"id":"finddecision_p1_2","t":"Ezabo\n\nI've started the decision points analysis, any feedback you guys have would be great.\n\nI've only had a chance to do the first few today as it's taken me some time to get to grips with the screen capture software, but I'll add a few more tomorrow.\n\nFeel free to add your own charts in this thread too, it's probably useful to have everyone's analysis all in one place so that we can learn from each other.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#2","p":1,"im":["08be94b344c41734f077084627b060689d3e19a4","f7d219b4c583cc467b2e4bf2a041748c9eb6379f"],"m":2},{"id":"finddecision_p1_3","t":"Ezabo\n\nAdding turning points 5-8:cheer:\n\nThe thing that's interesting is that you see the same things over and over, just depends which timeframe they are clearest in.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#3","p":1,"im":["7b57d8e12b5b217a05bbbbb908aef8285ff214cc"],"m":3},{"id":"finddecision_p1_4","t":"I'm loving this so far:cheer:","a":"—","d":"","n":"#4","p":1,"im":[],"m":4},{"id":"finddecision_p1_5","t":"Ezabo\n\nCheers If, your videos are great for showing how simple looking at this stuff can (and should) be.\n\nI won't do all the turning points as screen captures here I doubt, but here's one that I could use another opinion on.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#5","p":1,"im":["95ccde7f84948ec0f25e57a5e7aaedf059aad4ff"],"m":5},{"id":"finddecision_p1_6","t":"Harry\n\ngood stuff, i'd like to see more of this. i dont have an answer for the above, and i am not at ease with the thought that \"price overshoots\" but there are quite a few that stop in thin air.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#6","p":1,"im":[],"m":6},{"id":"finddecision_p1_7","t":"Ezabo\n\nNo, I guess it depends on just how precise you believe market dynamics to be.\n\nHopefully someone with more experience can shed some light on the question over 9 above.\n\nIn the meantime, these are the last ones from me today.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#7","p":1,"im":["a7abcb47c94f5a5b4e3b87366fde2896d9d03653"],"m":7},{"id":"finddecision_p1_8","t":"Ezabo wrote: Cheers If, your videos are great for showing how simple looking at this stuff can (and should) be.\n\nI won't do all the turning points as screen captures here I doubt, but here's one that I could use another opinion on.\n\nVery good presentation, you'll make a good teacher I have an answer for you..actually two. You could have figured it out by yourself if you had the M1 historical data.\n\n1554\n\nAnyway, if you look at TF 15M & 5M both are telling the same story, an ignored supply later was respected just as in your number 1 and your pivot line is inside the supply zone, but if you wanna be more precise as Mr. Ifmyante likes it then you have to check the M1 TF and voila...there is a demand decision point.\n\nPlease see the attached charts.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#8","p":1,"im":["dcc9b83ef70c52ab954f42cc82f0eca10b085366","4da574769c5ddb1170e647d14f6daa245